{
  "name": "vector_light_shadow_shares",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "§27 phase 4b: a lamp's shadow is that lamp's SHARE of the light on the pawn, not the whole of it. Six torches ring one colonist at four cells, which is what a colony actually does to a workroom and is where phase 4's arithmetic stopped being defensible — it charged every lamp the full darkening, as though each were the only light in the room, so six arms drew at full strength and composited to near-black under a pawn who is by construction WELL LIT. ROOFED AND AT MIDNIGHT on purpose: vanilla's Graphic_Shadow bails on roofed cells, so every shadow in frame is ours and no sun shadow contaminates the measurement. Four arms, each stating every flag: no lamp shadows at all, phase 4 as shipped (vector_light_shadow_shares off, which is not an absence but bit-for-bit the old arithmetic — the denominator pins to FullIlluminance), and phase 4b. THE PROBE PAIR IS THE ACTUAL ASSERTION, because an alpha is not something a screenshot reports: the peak arm falls x0.41 while the rosette falls x0.53, and it is the RATIO that says the light was redistributed rather than merely turned down. Pinning either alone would be consistent with the feature being half broken. vector_light_count is pinned because a scene whose torches failed to place measures a confident zero everywhere else.",
